"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act4_ch24.md — do not edit */

Object.assign(ENEMIES,{
 lacquer:{name:"Sister Lacquer of the Seventh Reel",hp:44,p2at:16,allies:true,
  open:"She is waiting in the document-house dark, a small precise woman lacquered to the elbows in hardened white, and she sounds genuinely sorry. \u201CSeventh Reel, brother weaver. Accidents and adjustments. The inquest drowns tonight and the papers burn \u2014 the Lady didn\u2019t order it, before you ask. Some of us protect her from her own patience.\u201D",
  p2text:"The lacquer cracks and she sheds it whole, like a wasp leaving a shell, and underneath she is faster.",
  moves:[{n:"Lacquer Set",kind:"stance",st:"iron",text:"White lacquer flows up her arms and sets in glossy coats.",tele:"The lacquer is rising \u2014 she means to set hard."},
   {n:"Adjustment",d:6,drain:1},
   {n:"Reel-winding",kind:"charge",text:"Her left hand winds an invisible reel, faster and faster, the air thickening around her fist.",tele:"The reel winds \u2014 the Seventh\u2019s seal-blow follows."},
   {n:"The Seventh Seal",d:12,kind:"release"}],
  p2:[{n:"Shed Form",kind:"stance",st:"flow",text:"She moves like spilled water with intentions.",tele:"Shell gone \u2014 she runs liquid now."},
   {n:"Adjustment, doubled",d:8,drain:1},
   {n:"Reel-winding",kind:"charge",text:"The bare fist winds again, humming.",tele:"The reel winds again \u2014 hastier, still lethal."},
   {n:"The Seventh Seal",d:10,kind:"release"}]}});


SC["a4c24_arrival"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY-FOUR — YAN SHUO'S NOSE FOR ROT`)+P(`The Azure Cloud arrives the way the Azure Cloud does everything: formally, punctually, and with its disagreements showing.`)+P(`Three grey-sailed barges at the guest moorings. A delegation of eleven: two elders you know by sight — Elder Wu, who signed Kang's audit honestly, and Elder Pan, whose halls upriver published their “irregular donations” with suspicious speed — six attendants, a records-clerk, and at the rail of the lead barge, in inner-court grey with a writ-case strapped across his back like a sword, Yan Shuo.`)+P(`He finds you on the dock and bows the precise bow of an inner-court disciple to an outer acquaintance, and then, straightening, abandons the whole performance and grips your forearm like a brother. “You look terrible,” he says, with satisfaction. “Good. Honest work shows. The alliance granted the joint inquest: three sects' seals, full powers of audit. The Court has agreed to host it.” A pause you could balance a blade on. “AGREED, weaver. Smiling. That is the first thing that has frightened me since the brackets.”`)+((G.bao>=3)?(P(`And down the gangplank behind the records-clerk, staggering theatrically under a yoke of provision-baskets, comes a big familiar shape that drops the act the moment he sees you. Bao. He sets down the baskets with the care of a man who has packed them himself, which he has, because under the salt fish and the bean cakes, wrapped in oilcloth and wax, ride the REAL ledgers: every copy the network holds, Kang's pages to Clearwater's schedules to the riverhouse rolls. “Steamed bun delivery,” he says, hugging you off the ground. “Don't squeeze. The filling's load-bearing.”`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The inquest convenes in the Court's own hall of records. Of course it does.`,go:"a4c24_inquest"}]};

SC["a4c24_inquest"]={t:()=>P(`The Court hosts the proceedings against itself with a graciousness that should be studied in academies.`)+P(`A white hall, excellent tea, every document requested produced within the hour: clean copies, beautifully made, and Yan reads three of them and sets them down and says, evenly, “These are fair copies. The inquest will see originals.” Madam Xian, attending for the Court, inclines her head as if complimented and produces originals. They are ALSO clean. Four hundred years of bookkeeping and not one incriminating line, because — you watch the inquest's clerks slowly understand this — the Court has never believed it was committing crimes, and you cannot catch a conscience that keeps its own confession in the open ledger column.`)+P(`The tribute is RIGHT THERE. Itemized. <i>Consignment, eleven souls, Clearwater seasonal.</i> The Court's defense is not concealment; it's jurisdiction, and arithmetic: the sects signed the charters; the charters fund the Loom; the Loom holds the sky; would the honored inquest prefer the sky DOWN?`)+P(`Elder Pan finds reasons to agree by the second session. Half the alliance's halls are on the tribute rolls themselves; the rot Yan smelled at the brackets goes UP, and up has a ceiling, and the ceiling is here, drinking tea with everyone.`)+((G.f.a4_truth)?(P(`You sit through one entire session with Suyin's arithmetic burning a hole in your sleeve: the proof that the tribute feeds the heat and the heat feeds nothing but the machine's own dead weight. The inquest could not use it yet if you gave it to them: it's a weaver's read; no clerk can check it. Evidence that only one living person can see is not evidence. It's testimony. You will have to make it CHECKABLE, and that thought is the counter-pattern's second seed.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Yan finds you after the second session, and his nose is working.`,go:"a4c24_rot"}]};

SC["a4c24_rot"]={t:()=>P(`“Three things,” Yan says, on the guest-ring gallery, low. He has not sat down. He does not sit down when his nose is working; you remember this from a frozen stream and a measuring rod.`)+P(`“One: Elder Pan requested the inquest's documents be consolidated aboard our barge for 'safekeeping.' Tonight. Two: the barge's mooring was reassigned this afternoon — a better berth, nearer the water-gate, very courteous — and the new berth sits in the outflow current of the city's tide-race. Three:” he holds up a mooring-pin, “this came off our stern line an hour ago. Sawn through and waxed over. The barge drowns tonight, weaver, with every original and every seal aboard, and it will be the most natural accident on this lake in a century. The inquest dies of weather. Honor goes home in mourning clothes and NOTHING changes.”`)+P(`He turns the pin over once and puts it away. “I have stood post on the documents myself since the bell. But I am one sword, the records-house has a water-door, and I am — “ the admission costs him visibly — ”out of my depth in this city. You are not. Where does the blow land?”`)+((G.bao>=3)?(P(`Bao, who has been pretending to inventory bean cakes within earshot, answers before you can: “The copies. They think the barge holds everything. They don't know about my baskets, so the blow lands wherever the BASKETS are, the minute anyone with white sleeves does the sums on my manifest.” He goes pale as he says it, and stands his ground while doing it, which is Bao's entire biography in one gesture. The baskets are in the trade-house cellar. The document-house. Tonight.`)):(P(`You do the sums the way Qiu taught you: if the barge is the loud target, the quiet target is whatever ISN'T on it: the working copies in the inquest's document-house, where the clerks collate by lamplight. The water-door. Tonight.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The document-house, before the lamps change.`,go:"a4c24_lacquer"}]};

SC["a4c24_lacquer"]={combat:"lacquer",
 win:"a4c24_won",
 lose:"a4c24_lost",
 t:()=>P(`The document-house water-door stands open exactly one finger's width, and the dark inside smells of wet stone and hot wax: someone has already started melting seals. Yan's blade clears its sheath with no sound at all. From the shelf-dark, a small voice, sincerely regretful, begins to apologize in advance.`)};

SC["a4c24_won"]={t:()=>P(`Sister Lacquer yields the way professionals yield: completely, the moment the sum goes against her, sitting down on a document chest with her cracked lacquer all around her like eggshell, asking, with real curiosity, “Where did a riverbank servant learn SEVENTH REEL tempo?”`)+P(`“From a man who kept your franchise's books,” you tell her, and watch the arithmetic happen in her face.`)+P(`The papers are safe. Yan stands down the watch he never asked anyone's permission to mount; Bao arrives with half the trade-house cellar on a yoke, on principle; and by lamp-change the inquest's full record — originals, copies, and the network's oilcloth ledgers — sits in one room under three sects' seals and one Reel-sister's professional, defeated respect.`)+P(`Which leaves the question the act has been carrying since the riverhouse: WHAT NOW. The tithe-arithmetic — who pays, who burns, what the heat actually buys — is assembled, checkable, and devastating. Yan's writ empowers him to publish it to the alliance the hour he boards for home.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`PUBLISH. Every river sect reads the Court's true ledger this season. Let the sum fight in the open.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_audit="published";G.yan++;note("Yan + 1. He seals the writ that hour. \"My master will call it reckless. My master signed Kang's charter.\" The first copies go downriver with the morning tide, and somewhere in the white city, a very old voice on ten thousand reels begins reading her own arithmetic in other people's handwriting.");},go:"a4c24_after"},
  {id:"c1",l:`HOLD it. Sealed, ready, a blade at the Court's ledger-throat: leverage for the argument you haven't made yet.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_audit="held";addIns(1);note("+1 Insight. Yan hates it and agrees in the same breath, which is what trust looks like on him. \"A drawn blade negotiates better than a bloodied one. But weaver \u2014 blades held too long get TAKEN.\" The record stays sealed under three sects\u2019 wax, and the Court knows you hold it, which was half the point.");},go:"a4c24_after"}]};

SC["a4c24_lost"]={t:()=>P(`You wake on wet stone with Mei's thumb on your pulse or Yan's coat under your head, and the smell of the night's outcome all around: wax, ash, lake water.`)+P(`Half the inquest's papers burned or drowned. Half — Yan's stubborn watch, Bao's baskets, the pieces Sister Lacquer's tidy schedule didn't reach — survive under triple seal. The inquest limps. The accident reads as an accident to everyone not in this room.`)+((G.bao>=3)?(P(`Bao sits among his scorched baskets doing the only arithmetic he knows under pressure: out loud, in food. “Lost the dumplings, kept the filling. We can still cook, right? Tell me we can still cook.”`)):(""))+P(`The audit will go home incomplete: enough to wound the tribute trade, not enough to end it. Sister Lacquer's apology, you realize much later, was sincere all the way through. That's the Court in one woman: the kindest possible hands on the worst possible errand.`)+SYS(`Defeat teaches. The audit survives at half strength (a4_audit: held; the alliance gets fragments, not the sum). +1 Insight.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Up. There is a counter-pattern to build, and the night just priced delay.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_audit="held";addIns(1);},go:"a4c24_after"}]};

SC["a4c24_after"]={t:()=>((G.f.a3_mei_present)?(P(`You find Mei past midnight still working: not on you; on the holding pavilions. She has, in three weeks, quietly become the consignments' physician: the Court permits it because the Court files her under HUMANE PROVISION and because nobody has ever successfully forbidden Mei anything. Eight sleepers fattening for a Loom that doesn't need them, and one herbalist's daughter keeping their bodies strong out of pure contradiction. “If you free them,” she says, not looking up from a sleeper's wrist, “they'll need to be strong. If you fail, they'll be strong anyway, and it will cost the Court more heat. Either way I win.” She ties off a dressing. “Hurry up, though. I'm running out of feverfew and patience in the same week.”`)):(""))+P(`The mountain's pieces are all on the board now: Yan's writ, Bao's pipe, Mei's wards, Ruan's books, Sho's listening, Suyin's warp. Tomorrow you stop auditing the Court and start out-building it.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The warp-gallery at dawn. Suyin is waiting with forty years of design debt.`,go:"a4c25_design"}]};